        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(acp): ACP session startup fails when backend does not advertise thinking config",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes #103802 — ACP sessions can fail at startup with:\n\n```\nAcpRuntimeError: ACP backend \"acpx\" does not accept config key \"thinking\".: code=ACP_BACKEND_UNSUPPORTED_CONTROL\n```\n\nThis happens when thinking is inherited from defaults/model profile and then applied to a backend that does not advertise a thinking config option.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis patch preserves explicit user intent while tolerating inherited defaults only when unsupported:\n\n1. **Track thinking provenance at spawn/init time**\n   - `thinkingSource: \"explicit\" | \"default\"` is recorded when ACP runtime options are created\n   - persisted in ACP session metadata as `runtimeOptionSources.thinking`\n\n2. **Apply strictness by provenance in runtime controls**\n   - if backend advertises keys and a thinking key is not supported:\n     - `thinkingSource === \"default\"` → skip (best-effort inherited default)\n     - `thinkingSource === \"explicit\"` (or unknown) → throw `ACP_BACKEND_UNSUPPORTED_CONTROL` (fail-visible explicit intent)\n\n3. **Preserve existing configured/model-profile defaults on capable backends**\n   - defaults are still inherited and applied where supported\n\nThis keeps compatibility and follows the timeout precedent while preserving explicit-thinking strictness.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- ACP sessions against limited backends no longer fail due to inherited default thinking values.\n- Explicit `sessions_spawn(thinking: ...)` remains strict and fails visibly when unsupported.\n- Configured/model-profile thinking defaults still apply on backends that support them.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- 13 files changed, 169 insertions, 3 deletions\n- `oxlint`: 0 warnings / 0 errors on all touched files\n- Focused ACP spawn tests that were failing in CI now pass:\n  - `passes model and thinking overrides into ACP session initialization`\n  - `applies existing subagent model and model-profile thinking defaults to ACP runtime options`\n  - `uses configured runtime=acp agent defaults before launching the external ACP agent`\n  - `uses configured runtime=acp agent primary model as an ACP startup model`\n- New manager runtime-control behavior tests pass:\n  - `continues turns when default thinking is unadvertised`\n  - `fails turns when explicit thinking is unadvertised`\n\n**Terminal evidence (commit 1b4ab4c):**\n\n```bash\n$ pnpm exec oxlint <touched files>\nFound 0 warnings and 0 errors.\n\n$ pnpm vitest run src/agents/acp-spawn.test.ts -t \"...4 ACP spawn tests...\"\nTest Files 2 passed\nTests 8 passed | 124 skipped\n\n$ pnpm vitest run src/acp/control-plane/manager.runtime-config.test.ts -t \"continues turns when default thinking is unadvertised|fails turns when explicit thinking is unadvertised\"\nTest Files 1 passed\nTests 2 passed | 19 skipped\n```\n",
        "branch": "fix/acp-opencode-thinking-config",
